@ [baseline_commit] 61188373a54dd23ef9fdf855e2c7cd1f0718d7a9
@ [parent_i03e_uuid] b13ea7b3-0ff6-4fcc-aed3-3eaec4a786c5
@ [obligation_compiler_uuid] 221f8904-678c-4447-b51d-244273383b13

& [Purpose] is controlled witness proposal
  + define the smallest meaningful roots from which later cases can be derived
  + define exactly what one mutation changes and which observation layers remain applicable
  + map proposed cases to I03E1 obligations without granting expected outcomes authority

& [SeedArchetype] is a reviewed construction recipe rather than fixture bytes
  + bind root direction family intended use completeness level source lineage and constructibility proof requirement
  + minimum_structural seed satisfies syntax needed to reach one target area but may be semantically incomplete
  + complete_safe seed satisfies every prerequisite needed for a named safe_pure semantic evaluation
  + actual_response seed is an actual ProcedureToolResponse value under one root-specific intended use
  + every later concrete seed receives a content digest and separate expectation review

& [LayerBoundary] is closed
  + byte operator transforms exact supplied bytes and may create malformed UTF-8 framing trailing data or duplicate keys
  + json operator transforms one already admitted JSON value and emits one complete value without duplicate keys
  + typed operator transforms one constructible Rust fixture through a reviewed builder or field replacement
  + relation operator changes one identity digest lineage state or cross-field relation while retaining syntactic shape
  + no operator silently crosses layers or reparses its own output to claim success

& [ByteOperators] are typed
  + BYTE_INVALID_UTF8 replaces one bounded byte span with a declared invalid sequence
  + BYTE_TRUNCATE removes one suffix at a declared token boundary or inside a token
  + BYTE_APPEND_TRAILING appends a declared second value or non-whitespace token
  + BYTE_DUPLICATE_MEMBER inserts one escaped or literal member-name duplicate at one object path
  + BYTE_WHITESPACE changes only legal insignificant whitespace as a metamorphic control
  + BYTE_ESCAPE_EQUIVALENT rewrites a member name to an equivalent JSON escape spelling for duplicate-identity proof

& [JsonOperators] are typed
  + JSON_OMIT_PROPERTY removes one declared member
  + JSON_INSERT_UNKNOWN_PROPERTY inserts one collision-free member with bounded value
  + JSON_REPLACE_KIND replaces one value with a representative of another JSON kind
  + JSON_SET_NULL changes one nullable or nonnullable target to null
  + JSON_ENUM_OUTSIDE substitutes a declared non-enum value
  + JSON_CONST_CHANGE changes one const-bearing value
  + JSON_NUMBER_BOUNDARY replaces one exact numeric token with below at or above operand or representation bound
  + JSON_STRING_BOUNDARY constructs below at or above byte or scalar length and pattern witnesses
  + JSON_ARRAY_DUPLICATE duplicates one selected member for uniqueItems behavior
  + JSON_COLLECTION_BOUNDARY constructs below at or above one real collection or resource bound
  + JSON_REFERENCE_TARGET changes one local reference target class without authorizing external resolution
  + JSON_REORDER_OBJECT changes member order only as a metamorphic control

& [TypedOperators] are constructible
  + TYPED_OPTION_STATE selects None or Some for one Option field
  + TYPED_ENUM_VARIANT selects one declared Rust variant
  + TYPED_SET_CONTENT selects empty singleton multiple or ordering-equivalent set content
  + TYPED_RESPONSE_STATUS builds one root-qualified status and permitted associated-field shape
  + TYPED_FIELD_REPLACE replaces one field with another constructible value of the same Rust type
  + TYPED_SERIALIZATION_REPLAY repeats serialization without mutation as a control
  + impossible bit patterns private-field bypass unsafe construction and post-serialization byte edits are forbidden typed operations

& [RelationOperators] preserve the changed edge
  + REL_DIGEST_ALTER changes one digest component while naming the value it ceases to match
  + REL_IDENTITY_SUBSTITUTE replaces one principal participant caller controller compiler verifier Observer invocation session call or procedure identity
  + REL_PREDECESSOR_REMOVE changes one lineage or replay edge
  + REL_GENERATION_STEP applies predecessor same at successor or overflow relation
  + REL_LOGICAL_TIME_STEP applies monotonic equal regressed or overflow relation
  + REL_PARTICIPANT_SET changes membership ordering or digest correspondence
  + REL_RESPONSE_SHAPE changes completed refused context outcome fault or prepared-request correspondence through an actual typed builder where constructible
  + REL_ZERO_CAPABILITY_ASSERTION selects provider external-effect and executable-operation counters or declarations without invoking effects

& [MutationCardinality] is one normative change per derived case
  + each operator declares exact preconditions target locator parameters and changed semantic dimensions
  + incidental canonical reserialization differences are recorded and cannot masquerade as extra mutations
  + a multi-change witness is a successor chain of individually identified cases
  + chain depth has a later finite activation maximum and every predecessor remains inspectable

& [ApplicabilityProjection] is operator-defined but not verdict-defined
  + byte framing failures expect later stages skipped_dependency but review must sign the expectation
  + JSON operators retain ingress applicability and declare schema typed semantic applicability candidates
  + typed operators apply only to output serialization or complete semantic fixtures as named
  + relation operators may be syntax-neutral and semantic-only
  + no operator automatically creates a CommonSyntaxClaim

& [ExpectationProposal] is explicitly non-authoritative
  + generator emits proposed expected ingress schema typed semantic and comparison dispositions with rationale
  + review binds exact case bytes or typed fixture identity obligation edges and claim witnesses
  + reviewer may accept refine split or reject the proposal
  + only later satisfaction signature admits the expectation

& [MetamorphicControls] test stability without asserting semantic equivalence globally
  + legal whitespace variants preserve accepted JSON structure
  + object member reorder preserves JSON object meaning
  + set and map source insertion order should project canonical BTree ordering where the typed builder permits it
  + first and replay case generation produce exact case identity
  + controls remain root and stage qualified

& [FamilySeedPlan] covers C00 through C07
  + C00 one minimum and one complete archetype per root plus actual response archetypes
  + C01 byte-layer malformed framing duplicate and limit seeds
  + C02 object-member enum const null and JSON-kind seeds
  + C03 exact numeric-token and destination-bound seeds
  + C04 collection recursion and local-reference seeds
  + C05 identity digest authorship and lineage seeds
  + C06 state token pass logical time transcript and replay seeds
  + C07 no-capability external-reference refusal and response-shape seeds

& [CandidateSelection] is deterministic advisory set cover
  + begin with all mandatory uncovered I03E1 obligations
  + candidate score is mandatory newly covered count then total newly covered count then lower mutation count lower fixture bytes lower construction cost and lexical candidate id
  + select the highest ordered score until no candidate covers a remaining obligation
  + uncovered obligations remain explicit gaps
  + human review can reject a candidate but cannot silently delete its uncovered obligations

& [CaseIdentity] is content addressed
  + domain-separated digest of profile root seed identity operator identity version canonical parameters output bytes or typed-fixture identity provenance and proposed mapping digest
  + expectation review identity is separate so review does not rewrite generated content identity

& [GeneratorDeterminism] is exact
  + fixed lexical seed operator parameter enumeration
  + no random source clock thread race environment file enumeration or hash-map iteration
  + checked resource budgets before materialization
  + identical input catalogues produce byte-identical proposal catalogues

& [Limits] are planned before activation
  + seed archetypes operators parameters candidate proposals successor depth fixture bytes and rationale sizes each receive exact maxima
  + parent maximum 4096 admitted cases and 67108864 aggregate fixture bytes remains authoritative
  + exhaustion emits no partial admitted catalogue

& [FutureOutput] is a proposal catalogue only
  + seed archetypes operator definitions candidate cases proposed expectations obligation mappings gaps and deterministic selection trace
  + no reader observations agreement findings coverage satisfaction pass signature or production result

& [AuthorityExclusion] is absolute
  - never: concrete fixture admission Rust generator parser validator reader semantic execution compatibility admission provider model service persistence network effect production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [RequestedDisposition] is preserve_then_sjs_then_form_inactive_seed_mutation_catalogue
